            Look at this entry for the verb lead in the Cambridge Advanced Learner’s Dictionary. What\n                     collocations could you learn from this entry? Underline or highlight them. Then write one new\n                     sentence for each of them.\n\n                      lead           @®      verb [1 or (led, led) to control a\n                       group of people, a country, or a situation: I think we’ve\n                       chosen the right person to lead the expedition. o I’ve\n                       asked Gemma   to lead the discussion. © Who will be lead-\n                       ing the inquiry into the accident?\n                       e lead sb by the nose         to control someone  and\n                       make  them do exactly what you want them to do\n\n\n                     See also Unit 3, Using your dictionary.\n\n                     Wer        to\n                     :  Use a dictionary to find three or four other good collocations for each of\n                        desperately    pain     wise     run\n                     |  Write the collocations you find in an appropriate way in your vocabulary notebook.\n\n\n                                                                     English Collocations in Use Intermediate     9", "char_count": 3215, "mean_conf": 93.02, "word_count": 414, "words": [{"text": "2.1", "x0": 300, "y0": 346, "x1": 372, "y1": 383, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "2.2", "x0": 295, "y0": 1043, "x1": 368, "y1": 1081, "conf": 95, "bold": true}, {"text": "2.3", "x0": 295, "y0": 1413, "x1": 368, "y1": 1450, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "2.4", "x0": 295, "y0": 1907, "x1": 369, "y1": 1944, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Exercises", "x0": 444, "y0": 157, "x1": 788, "y1": 222, "conf": 96, "bold": false}, {"text": "Underline", "x0": 440, "y0": 350, "x1": 636, "y1": 384, "conf": 95, "bold": true}, {"text": "11", "x0": 650, "y0": 353, "x1": 694, "y1": 383, "conf": 91, "bold": false}, {"